## What Was Done (Feb 21–22, 2026)

### 1. Reorganized V2 Flat Structure → +trackbench Package Namespace

The original V2 code used a flat `src/helpers/` layout. All 44 files were mapped into a clean MATLAB `+package` namespace structure under `src/+trackbench/`:

| Package | Contents |
|---------|----------|
| `+config` | `loadConfig.m` |
| `+detections` | `runDetections.m` |
| `+scenario` | `createScenario.m`, `loadScenario.m`, `loadScenarioCatalog.m` |
| `+tracking` | `buildTracker.m`, `initCVFilter.m`, `initIMMFilter.m`, `runTracker.m` |
| `+sensors` | `buildSensor.m`, `buildCustomFusionRadarSensor.m`, `buildIFFSensor.m`, `loadSensors.m`, `customSensorTemplate.m` |
| `+visualization` | `plotInitialScenario.m`, `plotScenarioAndDetections.m`, `plotPlatformToTrackAssignment.m`, `plotTrackSwapAnalysis.m`, `tabbedAxes.m` |
| `+analysis` | `analyzeTrackSwaps.m` |
| `+batch` | `runAllScenarios.m`, `ResultsRunner.m` |

Functions are called as `trackbench.scenario.loadScenario("name")`, etc.

### 2. Full Config Directory

All config JSONs were synced into `config/`:

- `default.json` — master config (scenarios_to_run, version 2.0, tracker/filter params)
- `default_reRunDetections.json` — config variant for re-running detections only
- `sensors.json` — 19-sensor master catalog (PSR, SSR, ASR, ARSR, PAR, TWS, AESA, FIRE_CONTROL, WEATHER, MARITIME, IRST, IR_STARING, FLIR, ACTIVE_SONAR, PASSIVE_SONAR, TOWED_ARRAY, LIDAR, ADSB_TX, ADSB_RX)
- `sensors_approach.json` — PSR+SSR+PAR for approach scenarios
- `sensors_fighter.json` — AESA+FLIR airborne
- `sensors_fire_control.json` — search + fire control radar
- `sensors_ir_fusion.json` — PSR+IRST+IR_STARING
- `sensors_layered_defense.json` — PSR+SSR+IRST+FIRE_CONTROL+TWS (5 sensors)
- `sensors_long_range.json` — ARSR long range
- `sensors_maritime.json` — maritime radar + sonar suite
- `sensors_phased_array.json` — TWS ground + AESA airborne
- `config/scenarios/scenario_catalog.json` — 18 pre-built scenarios
- `config/scenarios/clear_weather.json`, `storm_window.json` — weather profiles
- `config/trackers/jpda.json` — JPDA tracker config

### 3. 18 Pre-Built Scenarios

| Scenario | Targets | Duration | Degraded | Purpose |
|----------|---------|----------|----------|---------|
| `dasr_ideal` | 2 | 50s | No | DASR baseline, PSR+SSR |
| `dasr_degraded` | 2 | 50s | Yes | DASR in rain |
| `crossing_targets` | 2 | 60s | No | Track swap handling |
| `head_on` | 2 | 40s | No | Identity maintenance under merge |
| `high_density` | 5 | 60s | No | Data association stress test |
| `maneuvering_evasive` | 1 | 60s | No | IMM vs CV on S-maneuver |
| `storm_window` | 2 | 60s | Yes | Maximum degradation |
| `long_range_arsr` | 3 | 120s | No | ARSR at 250nm |
| `approach_pattern` | 2 | 90s | No | Landing approach |
| `par_approach` | 2 | 90s | No | Precision approach radar |
| `phased_array_intercept` | 3 | 60s | No | TWS+AESA fusion |
| `ir_radar_fusion` | 2 | 60s | No | Radar/IR complementarity |
| `ir_degraded_weather` | 2 | 60s | Yes | IR unaffected by rain |
| `maritime_surface` | 3 | 120s | No | Surface+subsurface |
| `fighter_intercept` | 2 | 60s | No | AESA+FLIR airborne |
| `fire_control_engagement` | 2 | 50s | No | Search-to-track handoff |
| `layered_defense` | 4 | 60s | No | 5-sensor stress test |
| `layered_defense_storm` | 3 | 60s | Yes | Layered defense in rain |

### 4. Supporting Files Added

- `scripts/runExperiment.m` and `scripts/runTrackingWithWeather.m` — top-level entry points (both from `trackingWithWeather.m`)
- `tests/testBuildSensor.m`, `testLoadScenario.m`, `testLoadSensors.m` — unit tests
- `docs/SENSOR_REFERENCE.md` — sensor type reference documentation
- `docs/V2_WORKFLOW_GUIDE.md` — workflow guide with quick start instructions
- `syncAdeptusFromV2.m` — sync script (re-runnable, copies V2 → adeptus)
- `.gitignore` — excludes `cache/`, `results/`, `.asv`, nested duplicate folder

### 5. Sync Script

`syncAdeptusFromV2.m` automates copying all 44 files from V2 into the adeptus package structure. It uses `mfilename('fullpath')` to derive paths (not `pwd`) so it works regardless of MATLAB's current directory. Always run with full path:

```matlab
run('C:\Users\Admin\Documents\RAINY DAY GIT COPY\V2_fusion_fixed\V2\adeptus-rainyday-tracking\syncAdeptusFromV2.m')
```

